  "decision": "crop-free-single-view-stopgrad-is-safe-but-not-equivalent",
  "interpretation": "Stopping shared full-view targets removes part of the target-chasing shortcut: final online, frozen CLS, and final patch-centroid accuracy all improve over the exact shared-gradient control. It does not repair the lower initial semantic intercept or the large global and patch-label gaps to multiview training. Doubling direct or patch-residual SigREG changes representation geometry without improving label-aligned information, so insufficient regularization strength is not the supported bottleneck.",
  "limitations": [
    "All scientific comparisons are seed-0 screens, so the effect sizes are not confirmation estimates.",
    "The result does not prove that literal image crops are theoretically necessary; it shows that the tested single-view objective needs multiview crops or another source of independent view diversity to match the retained reference at this horizon.",
    "No fine-tuning or official CIFAR-10 test evaluation was authorized or performed."
  ],
